## Root cause

`AgentBuilder`'s constructor (`AgentBuilder.java:141`) already applies the **full declarative configuration** via `configureAgent(agentServiceClass, this)` — including the `@ToolProviderSupplier` and `@AgentListenerSupplier` methods. But `AgenticServices.createAgenticSystem()` (and `createSubagent()` for subagents) then called the 4-arg `DeclarativeUtil.configureAgent(...)` **a second time** on the same builder. Setter-based properties were harmlessly overwritten, but *cumulative* ones — `toolProvider()` (list add) and `listener()` (composition) — were registered twice. With two `ToolProvider` instances each providing `activate_skill`, `ToolService` threw `IllegalConfigurationException: Duplicated definition for tool: activate_skill` at invocation time.

## Changes

**`DeclarativeUtil.java`** — the 4-arg `configureAgent(agentType, chatModel, agentBuilder, agentConfigurator)` no longer re-applies the declarative configuration. It now only does what the constructor pass couldn't:
- sets the default chat model inherited from the enclosing agentic system when the agent doesn't declare its own (`@ChatModelSupplier`/`@StreamingChatModelSupplier`), preserving the previous "ChatModel not provided for subagent" error when neither exists
- applies the `AgentConfigurator` callback

The 2-arg overload (used by the constructor) keeps the full supplier-based configuration, with the now-dead `allowNullChatModel` fallback removed.

**`AgentBuilder.java`** — added a public `hasChatModel()` accessor so `DeclarativeUtil` can tell whether the agent already declared its own model.

**`DeclarativeToolProviderTest.java`** (new) — regression test with a stub `ChatModel` and a fixed-name `ToolProvider`, covering the single-agent `createAgenticSystem` path (the exact repro from the issue), the subagent path (sequence workflow), and the programmatic `agentBuilder().build()` path. It also asserts the tool provider and listener each fire exactly once per invocation.

## Verification

- Without the fix, the new test fails with the exact reported error: `IllegalConfigurationException: Duplicated definition for tool: fixed_tool`
- With the fix: all 48 tests in `langchain4j-agentic` pass, plus `langchain4j-agentic-a2a` (11 tests), `langchain4j-agentic-mcp`, and `langchain4j-agentic-patterns` all build green
- `spotless:check` passes (note: I had to temporarily create a local `refs/remotes/origin/main` ref pointing at HEAD for spotless's ratchet to run, and removed it afterward)

