【assistant】Fixed. Summary of the change:

## Root cause

`runWithTransaction` in `packages/core/src/context/transaction.ts` unconditionally opened a fresh `adapter.transaction`, even when the current async context already held an active transaction in the `AsyncLocalStorage` store. A nested call therefore opened transaction tx2 inside tx1 — deadlocking any adapter whose transactions hold a dedicated connection when the pool can't hand out two connections (e.g. `pg` with `max: 1` behind Cloudflare Hyperdrive). This was inconsistent with `getCurrentAdapter`, which already reuses the active `trx` adapter from the store.

## Fix (`packages/core/src/context/transaction.ts`)

- Added an `isTransaction` flag to the ALS `HookContext`, set only by `runWithTransaction` (not by `runWithAdapter`, which wraps every request handler with the base, non-transactional adapter).
- `runWithTransaction` now checks `als.getStore()` first: if a transaction is already active, it runs `fn` within it instead of opening a nested `adapter.transaction` — mirroring `getCurrentAdapter`. Hooks queued via `queueAfterTransactionHook` in the nested scope land in the outer store's `pendingHooks` and fire once the outermost transaction completes, and an inner error propagates so the outer transaction rolls back as one atomic unit.
- Fixed an adjacent pre-existing typo: `let called = true` → `false`, which had made the no-AsyncLocalStorage fallback (`.catch` → run `fn` directly) dead code — `runWithAdapter` already used `false`.

## Tests (`packages/core/src/context/transaction.test.ts`, new)

A mock adapter whose `transaction` acquires a dedicated connection from a size-1 pool — reproducing the reported deadlock deterministically (guarded by a 1s timeout instead of hanging). 5 tests cover: nested reuse (single `adapter.transaction` call, `getCurrentAdapter` returns the outer trx), still opening a real transaction when only a `runWithAdapter` context is active, after-hooks from nested calls deferring to outer-transaction completion, inner-error propagation, and pool release for sequential transactions. **Verified all except one fail with `deadlocked: did not settle within 1000ms` on the un-fixed code, and all pass with the fix.**

