【assistant】Done. A self-throwing `global-error.tsx` now serves a built-in last-resort HTML fallback instead of letting the exception escape the handler.

## The problem

`renderAppPageErrorBoundary` is the last recovery layer: when a page error escalates to global-error, the boundary response is rendered through the RSC→SSR pipeline. If the global error component itself throws, the SSR shell rejects (`handleSsr` → `renderAppPageHtmlResponse`), the exception propagates all the way out of the dispatch pipeline, and the client gets a raw 500 with internal details — no last-resort UI, no middleware headers/cookies.

## The fix

**`packages/vinext/src/server/default-global-error-html.ts` (new)** — a hand-rendered static HTML document mirroring the built-in default global error UI (`shims/default-global-error.tsx`, ported from Next.js's `builtin/global-error.tsx`): warning icon, "This page couldn't load", "A server error occurred. Reload to try again.", a no-JS `<form>` Reload button, optional `ERROR <digest>` footer, and the `id="__next_error__"` marker (which the dev HMR client uses to recover via reload). Kept as an HTML literal because the RSC environment can't use `react-dom/server` — same strategy as `pages-default-404.ts`. `buildDefaultGlobalErrorResponse` returns it with status **200** (the boundary's "handled" status), `text/html`, the RSC `Vary` header, the edge-runtime header, and middleware response headers/cookies merged in.

**`app-page-boundary-render.ts`** — `renderAppPageErrorBoundary` now wraps the response render in try/catch. The fallback fires only when:
- the rendered boundary **is** the global error (local `error.tsx` failures rethrow — existing semantics preserved),
- the request is an HTML document request (RSC flight streams serialize errors lazily; the client owns recovery),
- the thrown value is **not** a control-flow signal (`resolveAppPageSpecialError` — `redirect()`/`notFound()`/`forbidden()` rethrow untouched).

The boundary's own exception is logged server-side only and never reaches the response body; the digest footer uses the *sanitized original* page error's digest.

## Verification

