## Root cause

The `_user_request_` route was registered and working — the 404 `"Invalid API id specified"` came from **region mismatch**, not missing routing. The API was created via the AWS CLI, whose SigV4 `Authorization` header pins it to `eu-west-2` in the store (keyed `region::apiId`). The data-plane `curl` invocation carries no `Authorization` header, so `RegionResolver` fell back to the default region (`us-east-1`), and `getRestApi("us-east-1", apiId)` threw the 404. This affected both `/restapis/{id}/{stage}/_user_request_/...` and `/execute-api/{id}/{stage}/...`, for REST (v1) and HTTP (v2) APIs alike.

## Changes

- **`ApiGatewayService.findRegionForApi(apiId, preferredRegion)`** (`ApiGatewayService.java:201`) — locates the region owning an API id, preferring the region resolved from the request, otherwise scanning store keys (sorted for determinism). API ids are globally unique in AWS, so the id alone suffices — this matches LocalStack's data-plane behavior.
- **`ApiGatewayV2Service.findRegionForApi(...)`** (`ApiGatewayV2Service.java:128`) — same for HTTP/WebSocket APIs.
- **`ApiGatewayExecuteController.dispatch`** (`ApiGatewayExecuteController.java:226`) — resolves the effective region via the new finders before v2 detection and v1 handling. This also replaces the exception-based v2 probe with a lookup. Unknown API ids still return 404 `"Invalid API id specified"`.

## Tests

Added 5 regression tests to `ApiGatewayUserRequestIntegrationTest` reproducing the report: API created with a SigV4 header scoped to `eu-west-2`, then invoked **unsigned** via both `_user_request_` and `execute-api` paths, plus a check that unknown ids still 404.

- New test class: **11/11 pass** (log confirms API created in `eu-west-2`, unsigned invoke succeeds).
- Full apigateway v1+v2 suites: all classes pass except `ApiGatewayAuthorizerContextIntegrationTest` (2), `ApiGatewayRequestAuthorizerIntegrationTest` (9), `HttpApiRequestAuthorizerTest` (9), and `WebSocket*` tests — I verified via `git stash` that all of these fail identically on the unmodified baseline (they need real Lambda execution/WebSocket handshakes unavailable in this sandbox), so no regressions were introduced.

